cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MIXA: Transparent Mechanistic, Equilibrium, and Hierarchical Statistical Analysis of SPR and BLI Binding Data"
message: "If you use MIXA in published research, please cite the software version, archive the exported reproducibility package (including analysis_code_sha256.json and methods/equations_and_sources.json), and cite the applicable primary methodological references."
type: software
version: "0.5.10-preview"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "MIXA Contributors"
keywords:
  - surface plasmon resonance
  - bio-layer interferometry
  - binding kinetics
  - equilibrium isotherm
  - single-cycle kinetics
  - mass transport
  - uncertainty propagation
  - hierarchical Bayesian inference
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  MIXA (Molecular Interaction Kinetics & Affinity Analyzer) is an open-source
  scientific platform and Python library for transparent kinetic and equilibrium
  analysis of Surface Plasmon Resonance (SPR) and Bio-Layer Interferometry (BLI)
  sensorgrams. It provides explicit reaction and mass-transport ODE/analytic
  models (1:1 Langmuir, two-state conformational change, heterogeneous ligand,
  bivalent analyte, sequential two-step binding, and Karlsson single-cycle
  kinetics), strict separation of measurement uncertainty (JCGM 100/102
  shared-control and stock/dilution covariance, measured-baseline propagation,
  profile likelihood, and parametric bootstrap calibration) from independent-repeat
  statistics and 4-chain hierarchical Bayesian joint repeat inference, and
  self-contained cryptographic reproducibility exports.
